Z||000000||terryk||11-07-2000||07:39 PM||||Does anyone have the Z-24 Digital Dash pinout? It looks like it follows the standard wiring colors for an instrument panel, but it would be nice to have confirmation.<P>Someone drag out their Chevy J car manual!<P>Terry||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-07-2000||08:18 PM||||First of all are you sure that thing works? All the cavalier digital dashes I've seen have problems with the flourecent display driver electronics. They log data but you can't read it. The problem can be constant or intermitant.<P>Second,,, GM doesn't put much of the dash wiring info out. They only give most of it to the few authorized repair centers. The dealer network can't even get it. What little information is around is from people who've reverse engineered the dashes. I haven't seen the actual shop book, but I have seen ALLdata for Fiero. Not even the pinout of the main connectors is in there. At least not in any way you'd recognize it. It's spread real thin over dozens of documents.<P>So far I don't know of anyone who'se posted anything to the web. I've been watching for that one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||11-07-2000||11:07 PM||||I should have been clearer. I'm looking for the IP wiring, not the schematic diagram.<P>Yeah, I've seen lots of comments about the poor reliability. I got this one for free and figured I'd play with it. I'm not sure it will find its way into a car yet.<P>Been playing wit a HUD too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||11-09-2000||01:39 AM||||This cluster is a remanufactured unit from 96. Hopefully it has some updates to keep it working.<P>I figured out the wiring and it seem to work. I haven't checked the outside temp meter yet.||||reg||1
