Z||000011||286SE'S||11-10-2000||12:30 PM||||The digital displays require a higher voltage than the +12 found in the car to light. They are not LEDs that run on 1.5 volts. The display power supply puts out -28v, +17v. -22, +2.1 and +5.2. These voltages are needed to light the panel and run the assorted A to D converters. This is all generated by chopping the +12 to AC running it through a transformer then converting back to DC with diodes and filter capacitors. The transistors that do the chopping are the ones that I found open. probably due to heat. There is a big heat sink all across the back but no venting to the outside. Since it can get very hot in a closed car in the summer and commercial grade transistors only handle 70 degrees C, it is no wonder they open up. Also found some degraded capacitors but that is the first thing that gets replaced since they dry out so quickly. <BR>TerryK: I am also interested in your wiring list. I have not tried; but does that dash fit in a Fiero pod? I should have know it was that one when you mentioned the outside temp display. Beretta and Grand Prix digital dashes have that too.||||reg||1
